# OpenWeatherMap API Integration Guidelines

Official Documentation Reference: https://openweathermap.org/guide

## 1. Security & Environment Configuration
- **Server-Side Only**: Store API keys in `.env.local` as `OPENWEATHER_API_KEY`.
- **Never Expose**: Never prefix with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` unless explicitly intended for static demo environments without backend. Always fetch weather data via React Server Components (RSC) or Next.js Route Handlers / Server Actions.
- **Key Activation**: Note that newly issued OpenWeatherMap API keys may take up to 10–30 minutes to become active (HTTP 401 error initially).

## 2. Core Endpoints & Parameters
- **Base URL**: `https://api.openweathermap.org`
- **Standard Parameters**:
  - `appid`: API Key (Required)
  - `units`: `metric` (Celsius, m/s) - Default for this project
  - `lang`: `kr` (Korean description strings)

### Common Endpoints
1. **Current Weather**:
   - `GET /data/2.5/weather?lat={lat}&lon={lon}&units=metric&lang=kr&appid={KEY}`
   - `GET /data/2.5/weather?q={city_name}&units=metric&lang=kr&appid={KEY}`
2. **5-Day / 3-Hour Forecast**:
   - `GET /data/2.5/forecast?lat={lat}&lon={lon}&units=metric&lang=kr&appid={KEY}`
3. **Geocoding API** (City to Coordinates):
   - `GET /geo/1.0/direct?q={cityName}&limit={limit}&appid={KEY}`
4. **Weather Icon URL**:
   - `https://openweathermap.org/img/wn/{icon}@2x.png` (Supported suffixes: `@2x.png`, `@4x.png`)

## 3. TypeScript Interfaces

Define weather data structures adhering to the following standard shapes (prefer interfaces):

```typescript
export interface WeatherCondition {
  id: number;
  main: string;
  description: string;
  icon: string;
}

export interface WeatherMain {
  temp: number;
  feels_like: number;
  temp_min: number;
  temp_max: number;
  pressure: number;
  humidity: number;
  sea_level?: number;
  grnd_level?: number;
}

export interface WindData {
  speed: number;
  deg: number;
  gust?: number;
}

export interface CurrentWeatherResponse {
  coord: { lon: number; lat: number };
  weather: WeatherCondition[];
  base: string;
  main: WeatherMain;
  visibility: number;
  wind: WindData;
  clouds: { all: number };
  dt: number;
  sys: {
    country: string;
    sunrise: number;
    sunset: number;
  };
  timezone: number;
  id: number;
  name: string;
  cod: number;
}

export interface ForecastItem {
  dt: number;
  main: WeatherMain;
  weather: WeatherCondition[];
  clouds: { all: number };
  wind: WindData;
  visibility: number;
  pop: number; // Probability of precipitation (0 to 1)
  dt_txt: string;
}

export interface ForecastResponse {
  cod: string;
  message: number;
  cnt: number;
  list: ForecastItem[];
  city: {
    id: number;
    name: string;
    coord: { lat: number; lon: number };
    country: string;
    population: number;
    timezone: number;
    sunrise: number;
    sunset: number;
  };
}

export interface GeocodingLocation {
  name: string;
  local_names?: Record<string, string>;
  lat: number;
  lon: number;
  country: string;
  state?: string;
}
```

## 4. Implementation Best Practices

### A. Data Fetching Pattern (RSC / Server-Side)
```typescript
// ✅ RECOMMENDED: Server-side fetch with Next.js revalidation
export async function getCurrentWeather(lat: number, lon: number): Promise<CurrentWeatherResponse> {
  const apiKey = process.env.OPENWEATHER_API_KEY;
  if (!apiKey) {
    throw new Error('OPENWEATHER_API_KEY is not defined in environment variables');
  }

  const url = `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?lat=${lat}&lon=${lon}&units=metric&lang=kr&appid=${apiKey}`;
  
  const res = await fetch(url, {
    next: { revalidate: 600 }, // Cache for 10 minutes (OpenWeather updates every 10 min)
  });

  if (!res.ok) {
    const errorBody = await res.text();
    throw new Error(`OpenWeather API error [${res.status}]: ${errorBody}`);
  }

  return res.json();
}
```

### B. Error Handling & Edge Cases
- **401 Unauthorized**: Missing/invalid API key, or key not activated yet.
- **404 Not Found**: Unknown city name/coordinates. Handle gracefully in UI with not-found states.
- **429 Rate Limit**: Free tier allows 60 calls/minute and 1,000 calls/day. Use Next.js caching (`revalidate`) to prevent exhausting quotas.
- **ODbL License Attribution**: Display "Weather data provided by OpenWeather" with a link to `https://openweathermap.org/` in the footer/credits.
